cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MAGI in work that leads to a publication, please cite it."
title: "MAGI: Multivariate Autoencoder for particle Generative Inference"
abstract: >-
  MAGI is a Conditional Variational Autoencoder that learns the joint
  phase-space distribution of particles crossing a surface in a Monte Carlo
  simulation - energy, position, direction and particle type - and samples new,
  physically consistent events at a fraction of the cost of rerunning the full
  transport. It is intended as a drop-in particle source that lets a long
  simulation be cut at a surface and resumed from a cheap sampler, which pays
  off when the events reaching that surface are rare for physical or
  geometrical reasons. The energy head is a gated mixture of a
  normalizing-flow continuum and fixed-position line components pinned at
  measured atomic transition energies, with a learned conditional prior that
  preserves energy-geometry correlations through generation. Version 1.0.0
  adds the prior refit, primary-conditioned models, a virtual tracking ball
  with a first-entry rule, and the Geant4 injector for the generated crossings.
